  "body": "**Stacked on #640** (#630, control-point posting, which changes the facing output). Review only this PR's own commit, `39ceb9c2`. The merge `c18542f9` brings in #640's latest tip.\n\n**P2 (#632):** lathe facing had two problems.\n1. Its first move after the tool call was a **feed** from wherever the turret was parked.\n2. Every pass rapided straight out in X at the Z just cut, **dragging the nose across the fresh face**.\n\n## What changed (`crates/motion/src/turning/face.rs`)\n- **Approach:** the path starts on the axis at the clearance plane, the mill kernels' convention. Its first move is a **rapid to the clearance point (rho_clear, clearance)**, then the existing plunge feed.\n  - Posted, the first motion after the tool call is `G00 X13 Z25`.\n  - The meridian rapid law (#103) judges this rapid. rho_clear sits outside the stock radius, and a clearance plane inside the bar is refused (`RapidInStock`) and not posted.\n- **Retract:** every pass lifts **`LIFT` = 0.2 mm (capped at half the stepdown)** up the axis, then rapids out in X at the lifted Z.\n  - The cap keeps the lift inside air the pass above already cleared.\n- **Profile Rough:** checked and unchanged. It already starts with a G0, and each rung exits radially outward at the top of its window, away from the finished diameter. This is recorded in the decision file.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/632-facing-approach.md`.\n\n## Golden diff (`fanuc-lathe/facing.nc`)\n- `G00 X13 Z25` is added before the first plunge.\n- Each retract `G00 X13 Z<s>` becomes `G00 X-1.6 Z<s+0.2>` then `G00 X13 Z<s+0.2>`.\n- The header's existing envelope-warning move index shifts by one. That fixture faces the part's own end by design, the same as on main.\n\n## How tested\n- **motion `turning_face`:**\n  - `the_first_move_is_a_rapid_to_the_clearance_point`;\n  - `every_pass_lifts_off_its_face_before_it_rapids_out` (3 stepdown/nose combinations, and no rapid slides along a cut face);\n  - the stock-allowance test's rapid assertion is updated for the lift.\n- **New app `turning_face_approach`:**\n  - `the_first_posted_move_is_a_rapid_to_the_clearance_point`;\n  - `every_facing_retract_lifts_z_before_it_moves_out_in_x`;\n  - `a_clearance_plane_inside_the_bar_is_convicted_not_posted`.\n- **Every new test fails on the old `face.rs`.**\n- **Gate:**\n  - camcraft-motion: 658 passed.\n  - app, 31 binaries and 277 tests: conformance, golden_cl, posting, every lathe_* suite, every non-thread turning_* suite, drill_prior* and project_roundtrip.\n  - Clippy is clean.\n  - After merging #640's tip: lathe_stroke 7, lathe_post 7 and turning_face_approach 3 pass.\n\nChangelog: Lathe facing now rapids to the clearance point before its first plunge and lifts 0.2 mm off each faced pass before retracting, instead of feeding in from the parked turret and dragging the nose across the fresh face (#632)\n\nFixes #632\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
